<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chidiaonga</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Chidyaonga</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chidiaonga was a leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maseko-ngoni">Maseko Ngoni</a> in the nineteenth century. After the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mputa">Mputa</a>, under whom the Maseko had moved north to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songea">Songea</a> area of southern Tanzania and been driven back, he led them into the highlands south-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-malawi">Lake Malawi</a>, where they settled around 1870. Leadership later passed to Mputa's son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gomani-i">Gomani I</a>.</p></div>
